hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"18500","And of what Sulayman ibn Surad and Khalid ibn Urfutah agreed upon: Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Jami ibn Shaddad, from Abd Allah ibn Yasar who said: I was sitting with Sulayman ibn Surad and Khalid ibn Urfutah, and they wanted to follow the funeral of a man dead of a belly ailment, so one of them said to his companion: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) not say: Whoever is killed by his belly will not be punished in his grave, and he said: Yes indeed."
"18501","Bahz narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, Jami' ibn Shaddad informed me, he said: I heard Abdullah ibn Yasar say: Sulayman ibn Surad and Khalid ibn Urfutah were sitting, he said, then it was mentioned that a man died of a stomach illness, so one of them said to his companion: Have you not heard, or has it not reached you, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever his stomach kills him, he will not be punished in his grave. The other said: Yes indeed."
"18502","Quran narrated to us, Sa'id al-Shaybani Abu Sinan narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, he said: A righteous man died and his funeral was brought out, then when we returned, Khalid ibn Urfutah and Sulayman ibn Surad met us, and both of them had companionship, and they said: You preceded us with this righteous man, then they mentioned that he had a stomach ailment and that they feared the heat for him, he said, then one of them looked at his companion and said: Have you not heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Whoever his stomach kills him, he will not be punished in his grave."
